2. **Medium bug — TOCTOU: key from stale snapshot vs voice resolved live inside ttsSynthesize.**
   Anchor:
```
        val result = try {
            CloudClientFactory.ttsSynthesize(app, TtsVoiceDefaults.TEXT)
        } catch (e: Exception) {
```
   Content: key computed from snapshot at run() start, but ttsSynthesize(app, TEXT) leaves voice="default" so the actual timbre is read from live NetConfig at call time; a save between snapshot() and this call stores the NEW voice's audio under the OLD key → wrong-voice playback if user reverts, and cache/voice mismatch. Suggest passing snapshot voice explicitly or re-comparing snapshot after synthesis before storing.

3. **Medium maintainability/bug — dropped triggers during in-flight run.**
   Anchor:
```
        if (!inflight.compareAndSet(false, true)) return
```
   Content: CAS-drop means any maybePrefetch during a seconds-long synthesis is silently discarded with the stale snapshot; a config saved mid-flight won't be prefetched until the next trigger. Suggest a pending flag set before CAS-return and re-checked at end of run (loop once), so the latest config eventually gets prefetched.

4. **Low performance/bug — wall-clock backoff.**
   Anchor:
```
        if (backoff.shouldSkip(key, System.currentTimeMillis())) return
```
   Content: currentTimeMillis is non-monotonic; NTP/manual clock jumps distort the 10-min window (backward jump skips retries longer than intended; forward jump re-hits failing synth every trigger). PrefetchBackoff deliberately takes injected time for testability — inject SystemClock.elapsedRealtime() instead (android.os import is fine here; file already imports android.content.Context). Also update fail()'s recordFailure call to the same source.

5. **Low maintainability — raw Thread vs structured/idiomatic concurrency.**
   Anchor:
```
