            {
                try {
                    run(app)
                } finally {
                    inflight.set(false)
                }
            },
            THREAD_NAME,
        ).apply {
            isDaemon = true
            start()
        }
```
   Content: hand-rolled Thread + apply(start) can be `kotlin.concurrent.thread(name = THREAD_NAME, isDaemon = true) { ... }`; better, a single-thread executor or a dedicated coroutine supervisor would unify exception handling (thread.setUncaughtExceptionHandler) and avoid per-call thread churn. Given checklist #4's structured-concurrency emphasis. Keep brief.

